  "claims": [
    "Mixed circuits have typed game/object atoms, pure value wiring, probabilistic boxes, sequence and tensor. A type family gives a possibly different state type to every atom.",
    "Only a fixed input catalogue supplies primitive rewrite roots. Context closure has four cases. No global semantic-equality or arbitrary normalization-path constructor is added.",
    "Whole-step support includes catalogue comparison-only conditions, both boundaries, and surrounding box conditions. Rewrites preserve declared multiset charges.",
    "Input-indexed kernel equality under finite declared support is closed under every mixed circuit context. An arbitrary correlated prior context and complete original input may be retained in the joint output law.",
    "An executable branching classifier covers every pair of mixed-tree rewrite positions: comparable prefix positions, or a constructive separated-position witness.",
    "Four ordered split-square forms and four context constructors produce a common-target diamond for separated rewrites. The executable commute function succeeds iff neither position is a prefix of the other.",
    "Both generated residual steps use a subset of the initial two whole-step supports. Under that union, all four edges preserve the input-indexed kernels in a checked model.",
    "Cached guards outside a change set plus new guards on the intersection repair the four-edge comparisons in a checked updated model.",
    "The MAC instance uses the actual original preparation/elimination conditional kernels and original game-vertex types. Copy duplicates the same sanitized full outcome; state and trace remain. Drop does not erase declared conditions or the charged assumption."
  ],
